# Build context for docker/Dockerfile (context = repo root). BuildKit reads this
# file because it sits beside that Dockerfile and is named after it; the
# patterns are still relative to the context, the repo root. It is not a root
# .dockerignore so that nothing at the root changes how Railway builds.
#
# The Dockerfile COPYs only the manifests, VERSION, tsconfig.base.json, client/
# and server/, so this keeps secrets, data and bulk out of the context rather
# than out of the image.

# Secrets: never in a layer, not even in the build context. server/.env is the
# one the server actually loads.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Customer data: RFP documents uploaded in development.
server/uploads

# Reinstalled and rebuilt inside the image.
**/node_modules
**/dist
server/generated
**/.vite

# Tests and their artefacts. esbuild compiles every .ts under server/src, so
# leaving tests out of the context also leaves them out of the image.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
server/src/test
**/coverage
**/test-results

# VCS, CI, editor and agent state; docs no build reads.
.git
.github
.claude
.design-review
.vscode
.idea
docs
*.md
*.log
**/.DS_Store
